# ZvenFit frontend files

## Astro pages and components (`src/`)

- Converted pages keep the Webflow-derived markup as it is: class names, `data-wf-*` and
  `w-node-*` ids are read by the Webflow runtime and the grid CSS
- Every classic `<script>` carries `is:inline`; `{` and `}` in text are escaped as
  `&#123;`/`&#125;`; non-breaking spaces are written as `&nbsp;`
- Comments passed as component children are dropped by the compiler; emit raw markup
  with `set:html` (see `Analytics.astro`)
- Whitespace between nodes in `src/layouts`, `src/components` and `src/pages` is part of
  the parity contract: do not run Prettier on them
- Pages export `sitemap = { updated, changefreq, priority }` for `sitemap.xml.ts`

## Static files (`public/`)

- Copied to `dist/` as they are; today these are two SVG logos in `public/images/`
- No pages, styles or scripts here: the legacy export left the branch in stage A2b. A
  file at the path of a route (a page, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `/js/*-config.js`)
  replaces that route in the build; `check-build` fails on it
- Fixes of the live site (lead form breakage, prices, legal texts) go through `main`
  until release A; new content waits for release A

## CSS

- Source: `src/styles/zvenfit.webflow.css`; the build minifies it with clean-css exactly
  as the legacy build did (`scripts/lib/site-css.cjs`), Vite's own CSS minifier stays off
  because it rewrites media queries into range syntax that old Safari and Chrome ignore;
  do not commit minified output
- a11y backlog in `TODO.md` Critical: focus states, contrast, touch targets, reduced motion

## JS

- Classic browser scripts in `src/scripts/`, no bundling, `window.*` config globals from
  the `/js/*-config.js` endpoints — never hardcode production URLs

## Scope

Minimize diff. One page change ≠ refactor every page unless explicitly requested.
